cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "On the Hodge conjecture for Fermat varieties"
abstract: >-
  We prove the Hodge conjecture for the Fermat varieties of degrees 33, 39,
  44, 51, 52 and 114 in every dimension, and more generally of every degree
  2^a 3^b 11^c, every degree 2^a 3^b 13^c and every degree 2^a 3^b 19^c or
  2^a 3^b 17^c with a <= 1, together with their products and the abelian
  varieties of Fermat type of these degrees. The key step is that the
  quotient of a Fermat threefold by the kernel of a suitable character is
  uniruled, by Batyrev's criterion for toric hypersurfaces; a second proof
  uses families of curves and a residue formula for their Abel-Jacobi maps.
  We also prove the Hodge conjecture for Fermat fourfolds of every odd
  degree, and determine which combinations of the standard conjectures
  around the Hodge conjecture imply it.
